	"claim": "For these six exact linux/amd64 third-party static images, the checked-in external-FFmpeg probe and closed audio plans admitted the matching ffmpeg/ffprobe pair, forced each admitted input through its canonical decoder, completed one bounded encode plus source-authoritative float-WAV decode for every listed format, and the strict WAV parser reproduced the pinned geometry and finite-silence PCM profile.",
	"limitations": [
		"This is Linux x64 CLI compatibility evidence only; it does not qualify Windows, macOS, ARM64, Homebrew, or winget packages.",
		"The 4,800-frame fixture is not sample-count-preserving for Vorbis in any tested release, MP2 in any tested release, or AAC before FFmpeg 9; the pinned profiles record those codec-delay and granule outcomes rather than claiming an exact round-trip.",
		"The images are third-party test witnesses, not application-distributed dependencies or a claim about their licensing, security, provenance, patent status, or production suitability.",
		"The silent 48 kHz stereo fixture does not cover every admitted setting or media corpus, and the result does not qualify releases outside 4.4.0, 5.1.0, 6.1.0, 7.1.0, 8.0.0, and 9.0.0."
